# Anatomical Provenance

This project is a forensic-grade canonical model. Wrong-but-plausible numbers are worse
than missing numbers.

- Every measurement, ratio or coordinate carries a `ProvenanceState`:
  `PROVEN` (cited source) > `DERIVED` (computed from PROVEN, method recorded) >
  `ESTIMATE` > `ASSUMED` > `PLACEHOLDER` > `UNKNOWN`.
- If you cannot cite a source, use `UNKNOWN` or `PLACEHOLDER` and say so in the docstring
  and in `docs/audit/`. Do not "fill in" a typical value from memory.
- `ReferenceValue.is_reconstruction_eligible` depends on provenance only; derivation
  method (`CALCULATED`, `DERIVED`, `COMPUTED`) flags `is_derived()` but never upgrades eligibility.
- `src/character_engine/data/anatomy/human_adult_206.json` is the canonical skeleton
  (206 bones + `ROOT_SKELETON` + `CRANIUM` = 208 nodes). Changing a head/tail, parent or
  name requires: a reason in `docs/reorientation/DECISION_LOG.md`, an updated audit in
  `docs/audit/`, and passing `tests/anatomy`.
- `human_adult_206_backup.json` is a frozen snapshot: never edit it.

```python
# ❌ BAD — invented value
femur_length = 0.45  # "average adult"

# ✅ GOOD — sourced or explicitly unknown
ReferenceValue(value=0.4489, unit="m", source_id="anthro_2019_tbl3",
               provenance_state=ProvenanceState.PROVEN)
ReferenceValue(value=None, provenance_state=ProvenanceState.UNKNOWN)
```
